21: The adverse mechanism is real. With assignments fixed, larger SINR targets increase coupled power demand; aggressors increase interference, formerly feasible links can hit their caps, and some users lose service. The [Claude fixed-assignment panel](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-codex-audits/parallel-20260909/LADDER-CLAUDE-2026-09-10.md) reports decoded instances falling from 24,351 to 22,046 at occupancy three, 30,800 to 24,561 at four, and 9,029 to 7,619 at five. These are meaningful counterexamples to a universal user benefit, although that diagnostic variant has the numerical limitation discussed in A7.
