115: Consequently target-mode decoding requires `F_d >= q × (N + I_realised)/(N + I_nominal)`, rather than simply `F_d >= q`. The code uses separate nominal and realised interference. A finite-sample, elevation-binned desired-fade quantile does not guarantee a percentile of coupled SINR, network availability or 50-Mbit/s endpoint delivery. Target-mode selection itself is conditional on feasibility and numerical clearance. The remaining strict-variant target failures already demonstrate the limit.
