The report is written and its source links check out. The central finding is that fixed-assignment control headroom is a valid diagnostic, but the current guard and unspecified information access allow gains that may not survive deployment. The report also flags a zero-power accounting mismatch and the fact that a fully unrestricted C2 optimum should not depend on which provisioning rule initialized the search.
