+The existing [common-fading audit](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/CONVEXITY-ADVERSARIAL-2026-09-10.md:98) already shows that channel evaluation and credited traffic can alter the apparent preferred configuration. It is a relevant warning, not evidence that this running gap will vanish. If common fading erases the gain, the original number was an unmatched comparison, not control headroom. Also, a desired-fade quantile is not a percentile of coupled SINR: realised interference is random too. Dividing a nominal target by `q` does not by itself guarantee 90% network availability or target delivery.
+
+**A gap confined to cap-binding anchors is a conditional finding, not a general control breakthrough.** Define cap strata from C1 before examining improvement. Report each stratum’s prevalence, pooled bits/joules, service changes and share of the total gain, under the corrected rule as well as the original. The relevant question is how often that regime occurs in deployment and how much aggregate benefit remains under that exposure mix. Oversampling adverse anchors can produce an impressive panel number with little operational value.
+
+For an additive accounting decomposition, use `ΔBₛ − η₀ΔEₛ` for each disjoint stratum, with the same whole-panel reference efficiency `η₀`. These terms sum to `E₁(η₁−η₀)`. Averaging stratum percentages does not give that decomposition. Beam-level correlations are descriptive: coupled interference prevents attributing a unique causal gain to each beam without an explicit intervention.
+
+A cap-only gap may justify a cap-aware fallback, a revised feasibility/admission rule, or reassociation of an impossible fixed assignment. It can still matter if sufficiently prevalent. It does not establish a broad learned coordination opportunity. If comparable service is infeasible at the fixed assignment, that is also evidence that the layer isolation excludes a necessary remedy.
+
+**Both provisioning rules need exact identities.** If assignment, admissible controls, physical evaluator, information and service constraints are identical, freely optimizing power and mode should give the same C2 optimum regardless of which provisioning rule supplied the initial guess. The two rules then supply different C1 references, not different physics ceilings. If each rule commits a different assignment or supplies a different BASELINE guard, separate conditional optima are legitimate, but their difference also includes those conditioning changes. If C2 remains constrained to a rule-specific power formula, call it a restricted policy-family search. A large gap confined to the defective rule measures defect cost, not residual opportunity in the corrected system.
+
+Do not treat “corrected” as a sufficient version identifier. Existing evidence distinguishes simple `Γ/q` division from an additional clearance implementation, with different committed results. [Provisioning audit](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-codex-audits/parallel-20260909/PROVISIONING-ADVERSARIAL-2026-09-10.md:94). Record source hashes, imported paths, configuration mappings, anchor/tape identities, rule variant and numerical residuals. Reproduce the declared law through the diagnostic evaluator before interpreting any alternative. The [recent runner imports a sibling source tree explicitly](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-arch-ws/scripts/run_prefix_ablation.py:34); inspecting only its workspace’s apparent source can review the wrong implementation.
+
+Threshold fragility matters here. Check physical SINR clearance and sensitivity to finite power resolution, channel-estimation error and control delay. A policy landing infinitesimally above an ACM threshold can exploit numerical precision without producing a robust link margin. Keep numerical correction distinct from changing a physical margin. Recheck all coupled beams after each update.
+
+**A large valid gap justifies investigating the control law; it does not justify three learned components.** First test how much is recovered by a corrected margin rule, cap-aware mode choice and deterministic interference-control or small mode-search baselines. The current control solve already uses `coupling @ power`; cross-beam dependence is not newly discovered authority. [Existing solve](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-ladder-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/batch.py:366).
+
+A better rule based on a beam’s own state and measured local interference makes this a control-law redesign. Dependence on joint state establishes a coordination requirement only when materially different actions are needed for states indistinguishable under the proposed local observations. Merely inspecting the optimizer’s global input matrix does not prove that necessity. Nor does strong coupling preclude a distributed analytic rule using measurements or messages.
+
+Learning becomes a supported direction only if a practically meaningful residual survives strong nonlearned baselines, the deciding information is available before action, the policy generalizes, and inference plus communication fits the operational deadline. Compare service violations, tail latency and total cost as well as mean efficiency. Learning can be useful to approximate an expensive optimizer, estimate an unobserved quantity or handle model mismatch; those are specific hypotheses to test. Nothing in a large oracle gap selects three components, their interfaces or their training targets. Replace the prompt’s inference from joint knowledge to a learned coordinating component with this evidence requirement.
+
+Finally, establish what the numerator and denominator buy in deployment. The evaluator credits decoded mode capacity; that is useful traffic only under an adequate offered load. If excess capacity above demand is counted as delivered work, a high-mode optimum can be economically fictitious. Preserve the declared capacity result, and separately evaluate demand-limited goodput when relevant. If every protected user receives a fixed credited workload, maximizing efficiency reduces to minimizing energy for that workload.
+
+The reported PA dominance is also dominance within the declared energy boundary: the [energy source explicitly excludes bus power and uses zero primary idle power](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-ladder-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/energy.py:87). It is not automatically whole-spacecraft energy dominance. Proposed OFF actions need special care: the dense endpoint counts baseband activity from scheduled transmissions, whereas scalar energy activates satellites using positive RF power. [Dense accounting](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-ladder-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/batch.py:491), [scalar accounting](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-ladder-ws/src/mcrl/physics_v025/energy.py:115). A new zero-power action must not profit from choosing whichever accounting path is cheaper.
+
+Before acting on the number, require one inspectable record containing matched reference reproduction, raw pooled bits/joules, the service ledger, information restrictions, cap-stratum exposure, solver bounds and a frozen causal baseline’s held-out performance. Eight anchors can expose a defect; they cannot alone establish deployment prevalence or narrow uncertainty by counting repeated users, slots and boundaries as independent samples. Preserve negative outcomes and use the genuinely independent sampling unit for uncertainty. The owner has already rejected a one per cent result: judge the residual benefit after these controls against a prospectively stated practical threshold, rather than letting an encouraging oracle percentage choose the research direction.

